Dear Hiring Manager,

Pebble's work on the 100\% electric RV trailer caught my attention. The integration of advanced technology for a hassle-free travel experience is impressive. I have experience building AI systems that optimize vehicle performance and battery health. This aligns well with the challenges your Software Engineering team faces. At Ayar Labs, I tuned a PyTorch predictive model for vehicle performance. I improved prediction accuracy by 15\% through better data pipelines. I also launched a REST-style AI inference service using FastAPI, which enabled reliable vehicle performance predictions. These achievements show my capability in building AI/ML systems and handling data pipelines, exactly what your team needs. In my previous role, I also worked with TensorFlow to create deep learning models that analyze large datasets. I used Hugging Face for natural language processing tasks, which helped in understanding user feedback better. I believe these skills will be beneficial for Pebble. In the first few months, I would focus on developing AI agents for analyzing vehicle telemetry and sensor data. I would also support the creation of predictive models for battery health and maintenance. I plan to leverage LangChain to develop applications that can make sense of complex data streams. My goal is to contribute to Pebble’s mission and help enhance the user experience in sustainable transportation.

Sincerely, \\
Sri Akash Kadali \\
kadali18@umd.edu \\
